[alert type=error text="Root cause: misconfigured connection pool limit in payment-service v3.4.1 — deployed 14:02 UTC, triggered at 14:18 under peak load. Rolled back at 15:02 UTC."]

[divider]

## Incident Timeline

[timeline color=red]
- 14:02 UTC: payment-service v3.4.1 deployed via automated pipeline — no issues flagged
- 14:18 UTC: PagerDuty alert fires — payment error rate crosses 5% threshold (baseline <0.2%)
- 14:23 UTC: On-call engineer Priya acknowledges — begins investigation in Datadog
- 14:31 UTC: Error identified as DB connection pool exhaustion — pool limit set to 10 (was 200)
- 14:38 UTC: Hot-fix attempted — config push fails due to validation error
- 14:55 UTC: Decision to roll back to v3.4.0 — rollback initiated
- 15:02 UTC: Rollback completes — error rate begins dropping
- 15:12 UTC: Error rate returns to baseline — incident mitigated
- 16:16 UTC: Incident closed — post-mortem scheduled
- 16:30 UTC: Customer communications sent to enterprise tier
[/timeline]

[divider]

