[divider]

## Root Cause — 5 Whys

[section title="Why Chain" style=card]

[timeline color=yellow]
- Why did payments fail?: DB connection pool exhausted — service could not acquire connections under load
- Why was the pool exhausted?: Pool limit was set to 10 in v3.4.1 config (correct value is 200)
- Why was the wrong value committed?: Config refactor in PR-2841 introduced a new key; old key silently ignored
- Why wasn't this caught in review?: Reviewer assumed the 200→10 change was intentional in the new namespace
- Why wasn't it caught in staging?: Staging runs at 2% of prod — pool exhaustion only triggers above 15% concurrency
[/timeline]

[/section]

[divider]

## Action Items

[table cols="Action,Owner,Priority,DueDate,Status"
  Add config validation test — pool size must be >50          | Eng: Priya   | P0 | Sep 21 | In Progress
  Load test requirement at 50% prod traffic before deploy     | DevOps       | P0 | Sep 28 | Planned
  Lint rule: warn if connection pool < 100                    | Platform Eng | P1 | Oct 5  | Planned
  Config change review checklist added to PR template         | Eng Lead     | P1 | Sep 24 | Done
  Runbook updated with pool exhaustion playbook               | On-call      | P1 | Sep 21 | Done
  SLA credit processed for Enterprise accounts                | CS: Jamie    | P0 | Sep 18 | Done
]

[section title="Preventive Measures" style=card]

[callout icon=🔧 title="Immediate" text="All DB connection pool configs now validated by CI — deploy blocked if value < 50. Shadow environment test added for all config-only changes under 50% load." color=red]
[callout icon=📊 title="Detection" text="New synthetic monitor fires within 60s of error rate crossing 1% (was 5%). P0 auto-pages 2 engineers simultaneously instead of sequential escalation." color=yellow]
[callout icon=📋 title="Process" text="Config-only PRs now require sign-off from team lead and a platform engineer. Staging gets 20% prod traffic replay from next sprint." color=blue]

[/section]
